	affiliations = {Christ University, Bengaluru, India},
	abstract = {Home solutions that unite the internet of things (IoT) and artificial intelligence (AI) offer a ground-breaking opportunity. This chapter discloses how IoT devices and AI algorithms can change household inventory management and security. The main focus is on sensors and AI-based analytics for optimizing data collection, analysis, and decision-making processes. Predictive maintenance becomes possible when sensors allow real-time monitoring of stock levels. On the other hand, integrated artificial intelligence surveillance systems, entry controls, anomaly detection algorithms help to improve home safety measures. Also, this project examines whether these home solutions can be used in commercial environments. By embracing this cutting-edge technology, the initiative emphasizes optimized inventory management, heightened security measures, and operational efficiency. For businesses seeking to merge IoT with AI technologies in future intelligent living spaces, this chapter provides useful information about them. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
