	abstract = {According to the World Health Organization, coronary artery disease—or any ailment associated with it—is the primary cause of mortality globally, taking the lives of 18.6 million people each year. Early identification and management of the illness can be crucial—in fact, it might be the secret for healing. Most scientists and researchers concentrate on machine learning approaches that accurately identify diseases for vast and complicated datasets, as their primary goal is to foresee the sickness in its earliest phases. Such methods are then applied to support healthcare. This work uses a variety of machine learning methods, including Random Forest (RF), SVM, KNN Decision Tree (DT), Logistic Regression, SVM, and Naïve Bayes (NB), to recognize heart illnesses early and minimize consequences. The goal of the project is to build an artificial intelligence-based apparatus for the detection of coronary artery disease by utilizing machine learning methods. We show whether machine learning can be used to forecast an individual's risk of developing cardiovascular disease. Data analysis is required for this application, which is regarded as enormous based on its around 88% accuracy rate over educational statistics. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
