	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85215006112&doi=10.1109%2FICEES61253.2024.10776906&partnerID=40&md5=8a434e735652dda73f14f599797b2c75},
	affiliations = {Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Coimbatore, India},
	abstract = {Addressing violations of traffic laws is critical for ensuring public safety, encouraging responsible driving behavior, lowering economic costs, and minimizing transportation's environmental impact. It is imperative to implement punitive measures for traffic violations. An AI model can play a crucial role in monitoring and issuing fines to those who breach traffic regulations through the alerts. High resolution cameras and sensors captures vehicular movements, while the algorithms analyze the footage to detect infractions. Hence, a YOLO v8 Convolutional Neural Networks model is proposed for the traffic rules violation detection and management. The YOLO v8 model is trained to identify major five specific traffic violations starting with Wrong Way Violation, Red Light Crossing, Over Speeding, Triple Riding, and Helmet Less Driving. The model operates in real-time, providing immediate identification of violations, thereby contributing to the enhancement of enforcement system and road safety measures. A unique feature of this project is the integration of an automated alert system. This automated approach decreases the need for manual monitoring, improves the accuracy of violation detection, and provides a robust mechanism for monitoring roads. The system notifies the respective person through email alert when a violation is detected, enabling them to take immediate action. This study highlights how artificial intelligence can be used to improve road safety and traffic management. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
