	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85205529473&doi=10.1109%2FINNOCOMP63224.2024.00080&partnerID=40&md5=199c0fac8cf0432d94737a6d710930e4},
	affiliations = {Techno Main Salt Lake, Salt Lake, India},
	abstract = {This research paper delves into the symbiotic relationship between Internet of Things (IoT) and Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies, and their pivotal role in revolutionizing crop management within the sphere of smart urban farming. Urban agriculture is rapidly emerging as a crucial solution to the challenges of food security and sustainability in densely populated areas. By harnessing the capabilities of IoT and AI this paper outlines a comprehensive framework for real-time monitoring and intelligent decision-making processes that are vital for the optimal growth of crops in urban settings. The core of this research lies in the seamless integration of IoT devices, such as sensors and automated systems, with advanced AI algorithms. This combination enables the continuous monitoring of various environmental parameters like soil moisture, temperature, and nutrient levels, leading to more informed and data-driven agricultural practices. The AI component of this integration is particularly significant in analyzing vast amounts of data collected by IoT devices, predicting potential issues, and making proactive decisions to enhance crop health and yield. The paper discusses in detail the methodology adopted for implementing this IoT-ai integration in urban farming scenarios. It includes the design and deployment of IoT networks, the development of AI models tailored to agriculture, and the establishment of a communication framework for effective data exchange. The results of experimental studies conducted to validate the efficiency of this integrated system are presented, showcasing significant improvements in crop yield, resource utilization, and overall farming efficiency. The paper also explores the broader implications of this technology. It discusses how the IoT-AI integration could be a game-changer in urban agriculture, potentially leading to more sustainable and self-sufficient urban communities. This study concludes with a forward-looking perspective, examining future prospects and potential enhancements of this technology, including the integration of advanced machine learning techniques and the scalability of the system for larger urban farming projects. This research not only demonstrates the immediate benefits of integrating IoT and AI in urban agriculture but also opens new avenues for future innovations in smart farming practices. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
