	abstract = {This paper summarizes experiences from recent projects demonstrating usefulness of Machine Learning (ML)/Artificial Intelligence (AI) in predicting State of Risk (SoR) of forced outages based on historical weather and outage data. Such approaches in predicting outage SoR may be applied in transmission, distribution, and Inverter-based Resources (IBRs) interfaced to the grid. The implementations are based on the use of power system outage records in transmission and distribution systems, and internal resource management systems in the IBR-interfaced third party owned hybrid systems. This utility-generated data is supplemented by weather and other type of related data that are typically available from government-owned weather or other related databases. We discuss the SoR prediction theoretical background, indicate the type of the data used for the prediction, and then illustrate the solutions as applied to transmission, distribution, and hybrid IBR-based systems. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
