	affiliations = {Global Research Institute of Technology and Engineering, Department of AI and Data Science, Raleigh, United States},
	abstract = {Competency shortage detection has been an interesting topic for human resource managers in particular in the discipline of workforce development after the success of the artificial intelligence field in Industry 4.0. Previously, human’s latent skills were being manually discovered which was time intensive and inaccurate as well as the detection was a low rate due to their performance being outside the scope of their management, with most HR managers receiving employee performance appraisal reports from middle managers, some using the information provided by their subordinates while others gathering results from other sources. Using the AI-Oriented Competency Framework (AIoCF), a manager can uncover the most valuable competencies and skills in a more formal and authentic way. This is a new model which has been extensively exploited by human resource managers in the world today. AIoCF will help in tracking each detail in skills, terms of competency, and adaptability as well as responsibility to complete the assigned work of their employees. AIoCF is a modern design for competency assessment based on current rankings and expectations of a new rank obtained through an AIoCF assessment platform and an intelligent approach for calculation based on professional skills from projects, knowledge from qualifications, or experiences gathered from working. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
