	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105000101108&doi=10.52202%2F078366-0003&partnerID=40&md5=4f5f0fb86efcd40768ebc0f4a8fd5181},
	affiliations = {Space Applications Services NV/SA, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Belgium; Telespazio VEGA UK Ltd., Luton, United Kingdom; SERCO Italia SpA, Rome, Italy; KP Labs Sp. z o.o., Gliwice, Poland; VSB – Technical University of Ostrava, IT4Innovations National Supercomputing Center, Ostrava, Czech Republic},
	abstract = {Earth Observation (EO) satellites developed, launched and operated on behalf of governmental organisations and by commercial companies have created an explosion in data availability. Delivering petabytes of data per day the frequency, and quality available from Copernicus alone where the free and open data policy has fundamentally changed thinking on the way we can use EO data. It was recognised that the transversal skill sets of AI/ML being used in other market domains could be applied to EO services and application development to revolutionize the ways in which Earth system data is handled for knowledge discovery. Observing that AI/ML capabilities were reaching a level of maturity offering the potential to facilitate and accelerate exploratory and predictive analyses of complex problems it was considered necessary to offer cloud-based platform services AI/ML development capabilities in an operational way to the EO science and application development community. AIOPEN is a project initiated by the European Space Agency in 2022 responding to the need to expand existing EO platform capabilities with new and innovative services based on operationally mature AI/ML software capabilities. The AIOPEN platform provides services for sharing, versioning and customisation of the various AI/ML resources and provides tools covering the full AI/ML lifecycle to develop, train, integrate and exploit AI/ML models in new applications. AIOPEN utilises cutting-edge technology and a cloud-native approach to address challenges in big data management, access, processing, and visualisation. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
