	abstract = {With the deepening of research on artificial intelligence (AI) technology in the field of computer science and the improvement of its social influence, the effective combination of AI technology and engineering project management practice has become a hot topic of discussion in the field of engineering project management. In the application research of AI in engineering project management, most of them use data-driven models to solve project management problems, improve data insight and improve the speed and quality of project management decision-making. Decision support systems have been developed on the basis of management information systems, but they have rarely been successfully applied in project management. The decision support system based on data warehouse is a new level of development in decision support systems, providing an effective way for projects to achieve real-time decision-making, thereby achieving synchronous, integrated, and optimized dynamic management of project progress, cost and function, and improving the timeliness and scientificity of decision-making. Therefore, this article proposes the theoretical framework and architecture of a construction project decision support system based on data warehousing. Then, this article proposes a deep belief network (DBN) evaluation method to evaluate the performance of the system, and the results show that the proposed method has superior performance. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
