	abstract = {Artificial intelligence is the simulation of human intelligence processes by machines, especially computer systems. Specific applications of AI include expert systems, natural language processing, speech recognition and machine vision. AI applications can be found in various fields in life. Water utilities around the world aspire to have efficient water management, thus, pilot projects adapted using AI, through having smart water management system. Applied AI in water management system by adaption of numerical hydraulics modeling system have many advantages as all hydraulics parameters will be available with a sufficient amount of calibrated field data such as pressure, flow, and node consumptions 24/7. Smart metering system is an application of AI, as it is a part of smart water management system, which can collect and communicate in real time the recorded data, smart metering system compound of Advanced Metering Infrastructure and Automated Meter Reading, using Smart Water meters with sensor/ RF to transit the collected data, data concentrator, smart system to analysis the data, with ability to detect any deviations such as unusual use, non-revenue water (NRW) losses, and water adulteration, in the water distribution Network. This literature aims to assess the application of Artificial Intelligence in water management system by implementation of Smart Metering System, through reviewing case studies applied in different countries: India, France, Australia, and Brazil. In spite of immeasurable benefits of SMS accomplishment. Smart metering system improved efficiency of water distribution network through, monitoring the flow, distribution, and consumption of water; enable real-time access to water consumption information and billing; increase water use efficiency and conservation. improve leak and fraud detection; and provide more accurate readings and data collections, while increasing the real revenue of water utilities. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All right