	abstract = {Due to customer-specific requirements and small batch sizes, the planning of manufacturing systems in the offer management phase in special machine engineering is characterized by a high degree of complexity. The submission of an offer (system design and cost structure) that is as precise as possible in response to a customer inquiry, with a low resource commitment and short time frame, is often decisive for the receipt of the customer order and profitability of the project. In order to keep costs and resources as well as the monetary uncertainty low, it is attempted to fall back on historical project and assembly structures of similar machines during the new planning. The fast and targeted identification of these structures is crucial, but requires the expertise of long-term employees. This paper describes a procedure for the standardized description of projects, assembly structures and components in order to enable a specific search by the user. Furthermore, an AI-based recommendation system is presented, which identifies and displays similar, equally relevant projects or machine elements based on the explicit search to the user. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
