	author = {Hernowo, Widi and Ridho, Rosif and Sunarto, Sunarto},
	title = {My HSSE&AI - A Novel Approach in Combining Safety Leader Program with Machine Learning Capability},
	year = {2022},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.2118/210912-MS},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85143082852&doi=10.2118%2F210912-MS&partnerID=40&md5=ecebe534d3475db79d3b061d74d9704c},
	affiliations = {Mubadala Petroleum, Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates},
	abstract = {Improving safety in a marginal offshore gas production platform using latest technology is a very challenging tasks as the cost of technology might not suitable with the field economic aspect. With this obstacle in mind and a request from corporate to participate in digitalization campaign, a novel approach need to be implemented by offshore team to meet the digitalization goals. The approach code name is "My HSSE&AI" in which combining Safety Leader Program, Mobile Operator Rounds solution and Machine learning to help gas production platform in managing HSSE&AI. The safety leader program as part of an antecedent system was created to disseminate, enhance and sustain safety awareness to all workers by allowing them to lead the implementation of safety programs for a one-week period at gas production platform (that already being implemented since 2013 by offshore team). This program then being combined with the usage Mobile Operator Rounds solution where the safety leader will need to conduct HSSE&AI inspections as per the schedule and in which "Mobile Operator Rounds" have the information at safety leader handheld mobile while conducting these inspections. Within the handheld mobile all relevant historical data of working area, equipment and instrumentation already being analyze by a machine learning based on big data being entered and provide analysis option for safety leader to define his decision at site. Through this novel approach, gas production platform was able to meet the company's digitalization while maintaining site safety performance and work management effectively. On the platform at any given time there were 30 personnel working on multiple tasks to produce natural gas and some of them rotate in weekly basis as safety leader. The site team made a diligent effort to follow the mitigations identified in the permit to work and maintenance tasks. With the help of machine learning based on big data analysis added artificial intelligence capability to help the team in managing work safely. This paper discusses the future implementation in combining existing safety program with the use of technology on a gas production platform as part of company digitalization goals and whilst ensuring safety performance in a marginal field. This novel approach is being was proposed for company digitalization committee to be implemented in a marginal field with a tight field economic calculation and at this initial stage being limited to Gas Compressions System as the pilot project. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
	author_keywords = {Big Data; Gasoline; Machine Learning; Offshore Oil Well Production; Safety Engineering; Gas Productions; Handhelds; Latest Technology; Learning Capabilities; Machine-learning; Marginal Fields; Mobile Operators; Offshores; Safety Performance; Safety Programs; Gases},
