	affiliations = {Business School of Sichuan University, Chengdu, China},
	abstract = {Based on the forward-looking, consensuality, self-adaptive, and parallelism attributes of Traditional Chinese Ethics (hereinafter referred to as TCE), a multi-layered and multi-dimensional study is conducted while the connotations of "sincerity", "faith", and "great harmony and unity" are sorted out, to form a new era of artificial intelligence ethics in the context of TCE. At a time of rapid breakthroughs in intelligent technology and the relative absence of ethical laws, we will search for a new AI ethics with TCE as the core and the way out. The research is based on The Hybrid Decision Theory and The Moral Competency Principle as the underlying logic, from the merit The perspective of the energy's general theory to discuss the Chinese traditional ethical norms of AI, the Chinese traditional the scientific content of four dimensions: ethical labeling, ethical decision-making and behavior, and ethical communication. At the same time, the research tries to explore the moral dynamics of AI technology and debug new human-machine relationships. To achieve the above, it is necessary to endow AI with profound TCE and form a circular kernel of "ethical renewal - technological renewal" to build an active "traditional Chinese ethics - AI ethics". -To do so, it is necessary to give a deep TCE to artificial intelligence, forming a cycle of "ethical renewal - technological renewal" and building a "traditional Chinese ethics - artificial intelligence ethics" active debugging mechanism. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
