	abstract = {Closed-circuit television (CCTV) condition assessment forms the backbone of asset management and maintenance operations for sewer collection systems. Condition assessment reports provide essential information decision makers use in asset management. Unfortunately, current methods are limited by human operators being required to watch every second of an inspection video in real-time, which contributes to a major portion of the total cost to inspect and assess sewer pipes. An artificial intelligence (AI)-based tool to automatically label defects in sewer inspection videos has been developed to assist in the process of condition assessment, and the technology is currently being implemented on multiple projects. This paper will focus primarily on the AI and deep learning processes developed to assist human reviewers in creating the condition assessment deliverables, and on a case study, comparing the AI-enabled CCTV inspection workflow as carried out in the field with the conventional (manual) inspection workflow requiring real-time data entry by a camera operator. Results indicate an AI-assisted workflow enables nearly a 100% increase in field productivity without requiring any capital expenditure for contractors or sewer agencies. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
