	affiliations = {Monash University, Melbourne, Australia},
	abstract = {The increasing popularity of Artificial Intelligence has contributed immensely to the digital transformation of the entire society and enterprises. Especially the outbreak of COVID-19 has pushed AI to an unprecedented peak. On the face of it, received wisdom has it that AI is positive and powerful, for example, AI can handle tedious and repetitive tasks more efficiently, control the risk more effectively, help people make decisions more intelligently. However, not each AI projects can achieve success. It is reported that 85% of AI projects confront the failure results [1]. Considering the root cause, a large number of articles explained that it attributes to the data, algorithms, and lack of support from management. This article, through investigating the performance of China Construction Bank's unmanned banking project, objectively analyzes the failure reasons which would be faced by the Chinese banking industry and general AI projects from a different point of views, including the policies of regulators, targeted users, the essential limitation of the technology, business goal and project costs, to help them comprehensively understand the risks and shortcomings of implementing an AI application. Finally, the article turns to propose some improvement suggestions to try to eliminate those failures. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
