	abstract = {The world's old people population is growing dramatically, giving concern as to how these elder people will get the good care that they need. Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies are offering eldercare the potential advantages for innovative solutions, computer vision, spanning areas such as sensing and sensory perception, smart homes, smart cities, robotics and human-machine interaction. At the same time, ethical and legal issues for AI application in eldercare are increasingly being reported as a social concern. This article updates and analyze the AI application forms for elder people by benchmarking companies all over the world, numerating their different functions in assisting old people's daily life. Ethical problems, such as the control authority, responsibility, false information, privacy and self-esteem, and the social well-being for the elderly, are conducted. In view of the numerous ethic problems arising from the application of AI technology, suggestions are proposed for better understanding and implementation of AI technology. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
