	affiliations = {Regulatory Affairs Recruiter, United Kingdom},
	abstract = {Advances in AI are likely to impact the regulatory affairs environment significantly, but this presents far more opportunities than challenges. A greater understanding of technology is clearly a requisite, but it is the softer skills, such as leadership and communication, which will be more crucial than ever as the complexity of these products increases. Regulatory candidates who have a solid track record in project management and leading a diverse team will be in a strong position for new, expanded roles. Meanwhile, life sciences companies involved with AI that are looking to hire regulatory professionals should be prepared to look at candidates from a wide pool, with a view to offering training and development for those with potential. If they do not take this agile approach, they may face skill shortages in the future. © 2020 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
