	abstract = {Site layout in construction is one of the most vital processes in construction planning because it affects the operation efficiency of the construction. Therefore, having the proper construction site layout could reduce the cost, shorten the duration of the project, and even enhance safety. In order to improve construction site layout, attempts have been made in the past through the use of Heuristics Method, which has limits in its application in the sense that it may induce combinatory explosion. However, due to recent developments in Artificial Intelligence (AI), the problem of combinatory explosion could be overcome. This research applies Genetic Algorithms of Artificial Intelligence to develop a dynamic construction site layout model. The construction site spaces regarded as a resource and are divided into several basic units in order to avoid repeated layout. The goal of this model is to increase the objective function value by increasing the range of solution, efficiency of space management, and decreasing the calculation time. © 2014 Taylor & Francis Group, London. © 2014 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
